      "content": "In your `orders` table, having `customer_name` and `customer_email` alongside `customer_id` causes a violation because both name and email depend on the customer, not directly on the order itself (which might only reference the ID). To fix this, separate the customer details into a new `Customers` table, using `customer_id` as the primary key there. Then, keep only `customer_id` as a foreign key reference in your `Orders` table.",
