    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok i get it. so the 'ordering' of the data is what matters. what happens if i don't do this and just leave the redundant data in there? like, what are the actual risks to the database if i just ignore the 3NF rule and keep it messy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ignoring normalization leads directly to data anomalies, which are severe risks in a database. The primary issues are update anomalies (if the customer changes their email, you must update it everywhere) and insertion/deletion anomalies (you might not be able to record an order until a customer has an email, or deleting the last order for a customer deletes all their associated details). This redundancy wastes storage and introduces logical inconsistencies into your data.",
      "source": "target",
